[{"id":"vector-predict-carry","itemId":"vector","role":"warmup","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">a</code>, <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">low</code> are vectors: each is drawn as one lane with its number inside. Here <code class=\"nobreak\">a</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code> stay between 0 and 9. <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> is 1 when <code>a + b</code> is more than 15. Steps 0 and 1 are drawn for you. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> for the rest.","explanationHtml":"<p>Add the two numbers in each step. 9 + 9 = 18, 8 + 8 = 16 and 7 + 9 = 16 are more than 15, so <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> is 1 in steps 2, 5 and 7. 5 + 5 = 10, 6 + 9 = 15 and 2 + 7 = 9 are not: 15 is the largest number four bits hold, so it still has no carry. When <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> is 1, <code class=\"nobreak\">low</code> holds what is left above 16, which is why it shows 2 for 18.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"adder4-small","source":"hdl/level-01/adder4/adder4_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"a[3:0]","path":"adder4_tb.a","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0011"],[1,"1001"],[3,"0101"],[4,"0110"],[5,"1000"],[6,"0010"],[7,"0111"]]},{"label":"b[3:0]","path":"adder4_tb.b","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0100"],[1,"1000"],[2,"1001"],[3,"0101"],[4,"1001"],[5,"1000"],[6,"0111"],[7,"1001"]]},{"label":"low[3:0]","path":"adder4_tb.low","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0111"],[1,"0001"],[2,"0010"],[3,"1010"],[4,"1111"],[5,"0000"],[6,"1001"],[7,"0000"]]},{"label":"carry","path":"adder4_tb.carry","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0"],[1,"1"],[3,"0"],[5,"1"],[6,"0"],[7,"1"]],"samples":["0","1","1","0","0","1","0","1"]}]},"answer":"carry","prefill":[0,1]},{"id":"vector-fill-wide","itemId":"vector","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">adder8</code> adds two 8-bit numbers, each from 0 to 255. Type the range <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code> needs so that no total ever loses a bit.","explanationHtml":"<p>The largest total is 255 + 255 = 510. Eight bits hold 0 to 255 and nine hold 0 to 511, so <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code> needs nine bits, as lesson 1.1's rule says: two 8-bit numbers need 8 + 1. A range counts down to bit 0, so nine bits are <code class=\"nobreak\">[8:0]</code>. With <code class=\"nobreak\">[7:0]</code>, every total above 255 would lose its top bit. No tool complains about the addition itself; only a line that reads bit 8, such as the one that gives <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code>, would get a warning.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-01/adder8/adder8.sv","firstLine":1,"totalLines":14,"before":["// Adds two 8-bit numbers a and b, each 0 to 255. low is the sum's eight","// low bits, and carry is 1 when the sum is more than 255.","module adder8 (","  input  logic [7:0] a,","  input  logic [7:0] b,","  output logic [7:0] low,","  output logic       carry",");"],"blankLine":{"left":"  logic ","right":" sum;           // the sum of a and b"},"after":["","  assign sum   = a + b;"],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"// Adds two 8-bit numbers a and b, each 0 to 255. low is the sum's eight","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// low bits, and carry is 1 when the sum is more than 255.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"adder8","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"7","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] a,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"input","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"7","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] b,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" [","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"7","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"] low,","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"output","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":"       carry","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"text":");","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  logic","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":" sum;           ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"// the sum of a and b","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}]},"after":[[],[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" sum   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" a ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"+","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" b;","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]]},"accept":["[8:0]"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The missing range"},{"id":"vector-fill-bit","itemId":"vector","role":"core","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">adder8</code>'s <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> must be 1 exactly when the total is more than 255. Type the bit-select of <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code> that gives it.","explanationHtml":"<p>Bit 8 of the nine-bit sum is worth 256: each bit is worth twice the one below it. Every total from 256 to 510 has it set, and every total from 0 to 255 has it clear, so <code class=\"nobreak\">sum[8]</code> is the carry. The eight bits below it, <code class=\"nobreak\">sum[7:0]</code>, are <code class=\"nobreak\">low</code>.</p>","type":"fill","file":"hdl/level-01/adder8/adder8.sv","firstLine":12,"totalLines":14,"before":["  assign low   = sum[7:0];"],"blankLine":{"left":"  assign carry = ","right":";"},"after":[],"highlighted":{"before":[[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" low   ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" sum[","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"7","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":":","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":"0","color":"var(--code-token-constant)","bold":false},{"text":"];","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]],"blankLine":{"left":[{"text":"  ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"assign","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" carry ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"=","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":false},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],"right":[{"text":";","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}]},"after":[]},"accept":["sum[8]","sum[8:8]"],"caseSensitive":true,"blankLabel":"The missing bit-select"},{"id":"vector-predict-hex","itemId":"vector","role":"stretch","promptHtml":"<code class=\"nobreak\">a</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code> are drawn in hexadecimal, and they use the digits A to F. <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> is 1 when <code>a + b</code> is more than 15. Set <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> for every step.","explanationHtml":"<p>A is 10, C is 12, D is 13 and F is 15. The sums are F + 1 = 16, 7 + 7 = 14, A + 5 = 15, C + 4 = 16, F + F = 30, 6 + A = 16, D + 2 = 15 and 0 + F = 15, so <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> is 1 in steps 0, 3, 4 and 5. Three of the sums are exactly 15, the most four bits hold, so they carry nothing. <code class=\"nobreak\">low</code> shows E in step 1 (14) and in step 4 (30): only <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> tells them apart.</p>","type":"waveform","wave":{"id":"adder4-hex","source":"hdl/level-01/adder4/adder4_tb.sv","timescale":"1ps","period":10000,"periodText":"10 ns","unit":"step","cycles":8,"signals":[{"label":"a[3:0]","path":"adder4_tb.a","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1111"],[1,"0111"],[2,"1010"],[3,"1100"],[4,"1111"],[5,"0110"],[6,"1101"],[7,"0000"]]},{"label":"b[3:0]","path":"adder4_tb.b","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0001"],[1,"0111"],[2,"0101"],[3,"0100"],[4,"1111"],[5,"1010"],[6,"0010"],[7,"1111"]]},{"label":"low[3:0]","path":"adder4_tb.low","width":4,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"0000"],[1,"1110"],[2,"1111"],[3,"0000"],[4,"1110"],[5,"0000"],[6,"1111"]]},{"label":"carry","path":"adder4_tb.carry","width":1,"role":"signal","changes":[[0,"1"],[1,"0"],[3,"1"],[6,"0"]],"samples":["1","0","0","1","1","1","0","0"]}]},"answer":"carry"},{"id":"vector-find-bug","itemId":"vector","role":"core","promptHtml":"This adder should work like lesson 1.1's: <code class=\"nobreak\">low</code> is the four low bits of <code>a + b</code>, and <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> is 1 when the sum is more than 15. Verilator warns that the code asks for a bit of <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code> that does not exist. Pick the line that is wrong.","explanationHtml":"<p>The declaration gives <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code> four bits, 0 to 15, but <code>a + b</code> can reach 30, which needs five. Verilator reports the problem at the <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> line, because that is where the code asks for bit 4, which a four-bit <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code> does not have. That line asks for the right bit: in a five-bit sum, bit 4 is the carry. What is wrong is the declaration that left it out. Rewriting the <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> line could hide the warning, but <code class=\"nobreak\">sum</code> would still not hold what its comment promises, the sum of <code class=\"nobreak\">a</code> and <code class=\"nobreak\">b</code>. In a simulation, bit 4 of a four-bit vector reads as unknown, so <code class=\"nobreak\">carry</code> would be wrong in every step.</p>","type":"find-bug","file":"hdl/level-01/adder4_bug/adder4_bug.sv","firstLine":1,"lines":[[{"text":"// Adds two 4-bit numbers a and b. low is the sum's four low bits, and","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"// carry is 1 when the sum is more than 15.","color":"var(--code-token-comment)","bold":false}],[{"text":"module","color":"var(--code-token-keyword)","bold":true},{"text":" ","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false},{"text":"adder4_bug","color":"var(--code-token-function)","bold":false},{"text":" (","color":"var(--code-foreground)","bold":false}],[{"tex